# Cloudflare Pages rewrites.
#
# This file used to be one line: `/* /index.html 200`. That is the standard
# single-page-app fallback, and on this site it was actively harmful.
#
# Every real route here is prerendered to its own index.html by
# script/prerender.ts, so the fallback was not needed to serve them. What it
# did instead was answer 200 OK to every URL that does not exist. Google calls
# that a soft 404: maxdoubin.com/asdf returned a page, so the crawler treated
# a bottomless supply of junk URLs as real, spent crawl budget on them, and
# had to guess which of the 331 real pages were worth indexing. A 404 that
# says 200 is one of the few things that will stop a small site being indexed
# properly.
#
# So the fallback is now enumerated. Only routes that have NO prerendered file
# are rewritten to the shell; everything else is served as its own static
# document, and anything matching neither falls through to 404.html, which
# Cloudflare Pages serves with a real 404 status.
#
# scripts-ci/check-spa-routes.mjs fails the build if a route in App.tsx is
# neither prerendered nor listed here, so adding a route without adding it in
# one of those two places cannot ship a page that 404s at people.

# One site, one hostname.
#
# www.maxdoubin.com answers 200 today, so every page exists at two addresses.
# The canonical tag points at the apex and Google usually works it out, but
# "usually" costs crawl budget on a site trying to get 236 articles indexed.
# An absolute source URL makes this a host-level redirect rather than a path
# rule, and :splat carries the rest of the path across.
https://www.maxdoubin.com/* https://maxdoubin.com/:splat 301

# The simulator's internal dashboards. Canvas-driven, nothing meaningful to
# prerender, and noindex in _headers so crawl budget goes to the writing.
# /game itself IS prerendered now: it is one of the most distinctive things
# here and deserves a real shot at ranking.
/noc             /index.html   200
/network         /index.html   200
/floor           /index.html   200
/incidents       /index.html   200
/build           /index.html   200

# The pre-redesign site, kept reachable for old inbound links.
/legacy          /index.html   200
/legacy/game     /index.html   200
/legacy/blog     /index.html   200
/legacy/blog/*   /index.html   200
/legacy/projects /index.html   200
/legacy/contact  /index.html   200
